{"archetypes":[{"name":"telemetry","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds a new timing-ledger row type and JSON aggregation path where column alignment and interval matching are easy to get subtly wrong.","prompt_body":"Inspect the timing-ledger.sh record-round implementation and timing-report.sh JSON aggregation. Focus on TSV column alignment, validation, duplicate round handling, sorting by round number, JSON construction, and whether nested child steps attach rounds to the correct step interval. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"handoff","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Deferred Step 5 and design MAV paths span scripts and SKILL.md orchestration prose, so integration regressions may hide between surfaces.","prompt_body":"Review the deferred handoff timing paths for main-agent-vote-required, coder-main-agent-required, stalls, resumes, and mav-resume-past-cap. Check that round starts are persisted, counts are refreshed before recording, round rows are emitted before Step 7 marks, and no path double-records or drops wall time. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bash-portability","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"New and modified shell scripts use awk, grep, jq, mktemp, arrays, and bash conditionals that need to remain portable to the repo's Bash 3.2 target.","prompt_body":"Audit the new shell code for Bash 3.2 compatibility and robust POSIX-tool usage. Pay attention to regex conditionals, awk behavior, mktemp patterns, set -e interactions, temporary-file replacement, quoting, and command availability fallbacks. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"counting","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The feature depends on parsing accepted, rejected, and OOS counts from several artifact formats with precedence and fallback rules.","prompt_body":"Examine the implement and design round-timing helper scripts' count extraction logic. Verify precedence between review-tally.env, markdown fallbacks, review-summary.json, and voting-tally.md, including rejected heading formats, grep -n prefixes, zero-count handling, and accepted-only OOS semantics. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"publish-artifacts","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Design publishing now renders and curates timing-report-final artifacts just before log publication, creating stale-file and failure-mode risk.","prompt_body":"Investigate the design publish changes around fresh timing JSON rendering and artifact cleanup. Check ordering relative to design-log-publish.sh, handling of stale timing-report-final sidecars, temp stderr containment, jq validation failures, warning emission, and whether failed renders can accidentally publish stale or partial data. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
